  "text": "olivia: Quick mock for an inline threshold editor on the SLO details page \u2014 looking for a fast gut-check on keyboard flow, preview state, and how suppression info surfaces. figma: https://figma.redwood/mock-inline-thresholds :eyes:\n\nsam: Nice start. main worry is context loss when the editor opens inline. Feels like it can push other content off screen on narrow viewports. Could we try a slide-over/drawer instead of full inline expansion?\n\nanya: Agree with Sam re: preserving context. If we keep inline, we need to ensure focus stays within the editor (focus trap) and that Escape cancels. Also we should announce success/errors via aria-live so screen readers know what happened.\n\nkevin: Copy nits: change generic \"Apply\" to \"Save threshold\" and \"Cancel\" -> \"Discard changes\". Clears ambiguity for non-technical users. Also the threshold label reads \"p99 latency\" \u2014 add tooltip explaining p99 calc.\n\ntariq: Implementation note: current prototype uses contenteditable spans \u2014 that's a11y minefield. I'll switch to semantic <input>/<select> controls so native keyboard + screenreader behavior works. We should add aria-describedby ids for the tooltip and error text.\n\npri: For the notification preview: can we show a mapping preview line like \"If triggered -> PagerDuty (oncall) > Email (primary-team)\"? Folks get confused which channel is primary vs fallback. Also add a small \"Send test notification\" button next to the preview (disabled until rule saved).\n\nsam: Test button is \ud83d\udc4d but it needs rate-limiting and a modal confirming recipients before sending. Also show last 30-day delivery success rate in the preview (tiny meter).\n\nanya: UI contrast concern: the channel pills in the mock are light-gray text on slightly lighter bg \u2014 fails 4.5:1. Please bump the text contrast and add a clear focus ring for keyboard users (not just outline: none).\n\nkevin: UX question: suppression terminology confuses product folks. Maybe change copy from \"Suppression window\" to \"Mute window\" and add microcopy: \"Temporarily mute notifications for this SLO\". Also add a help icon that opens a short explainer.\n\nolivia: Good catch \u2014 I can try both label options in the next pass. Also considering an inline condensed state that shows \"Muted until 3:00PM\" with an edit icon that opens the editor. Less intrusive than a full drawer.\n\ntariq: For keyboard nav, ensure the condensed state is focusable and Enter opens the editor. Also we should preserve scroll position when editor opens/closes so users don't get dumped to top of page.\n\npri: One more on preview copy: change \"Preview recipients\" -> \"Who will be notified\" \u2014 plain language helps non-engineers.\n\nkevin: Accessibility checklist for next mock: 1) semantic inputs 2) aria-live for toasts 3) focus trap + visible focus styles 4) color contrast fixes 5) keyboard single-key shortcuts documented (e.g., Esc to cancel).\n\nolivia: I'll iterate and post a second frame later today. Will try the condensed focusable pill + drawer fallback approach, update copy per Kevin/Pri, and fix contrast.\n\ndesign-bot: Reminder \u2014 design review sync at 3pm today. Add updates to the Figma thread before then. :spiral_calendar_pad:\n\nsam: thanks \u2014 I'll validate responsive behavior on mobile widths after the update.\n\nolivia: Uploaded v2: https://figma.redwood/mock-inline-thresholds/v2 \u2014 changed \"Apply\" -> \"Save threshold\", added condensed mute pill, and a small preview card that lists channels + last-30d success. can we get quick pass on the pill contrast?\n\nanya: v2 looks much better. Contrast on pill is okay now, focus ring visible. One remaining tweak: the live region currently reads the full message \"Threshold saved successfully\" at once; prefer a shorter atomic message for screen readers like \"Threshold saved.\" and then separate status details in an aria-describedby region.\n\ntariq: I'll coordinate with Olivia on the HTML ids. small code example for the live region we can use:\n\n```\n<div id=\"toast\" aria-live=\"polite\">Threshold saved.</div>\n<div id=\"toast-details\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Evaluated 3 queries, next check in 5m.</div>\n```\n\nkevin: Looks good. last copy tweak: change header \"Notification preview\" -> \"Who gets notified\" (aligns with Pri).\n\nolivia: Done. Thanks all \u2014 merging these into the next dev PR. I'll ping the channel when the frontend branch is open for review. :sparkles:",
